    <string name="rules_title">Rules</string>
    <string name="welcome_title">Place one, twist one</string>
    <string name="rules_1">Black goes first. Each turn, start by placing a marble in any empty dimple.</string>
    <string name="rules_2">Then you must twist one of the four small blocks a quarter turn, either way. An empty block counts too.</string>
    <string name="rules_3">Five in a row, any direction, wins. A five that appears after the twist counts. Five right after placing wins on the spot, no twist needed.</string>
    <string name="rules_4">If both sides have five after a twist, it\'s a draw. All 36 dimples full with no five is a draw too.</string>
    <string name="rules_mistakes">Common slips</string>
    <string name="mistake_1">Staring at where to place while their three sit next to a block you could twist apart. Think twist first, then place.</string>
    <string name="mistake_2">A twist moves your marbles too. Rotate it in your head before you place.</string>
    <string name="mistake_3">The win is checked after the twist, not just after placing. When they\'re one short, look for the block that fills it with one turn.</string>
    <string name="mistake_4">Pinching the moment your eyes land. Settle on the dimple first; you can tap the marble back before you twist.</string>
    <string name="symmetry_title">What does “no twist needed” mean?</string>
    <string name="symmetry_1">Sometimes no twist changes anything, like a first marble in a block\'s centre.</string>
    <string name="symmetry_2">We skip the twist for you then, and say so in the status line.</string>
